Add per-species/size fee matrix (Dog Large-Aggressive/Small, Cat, Other)

Extends per-nigam fees with an optional 4-bucket matrix so each Nigam can
charge different rates for Large/Aggressive vs Small dogs, plus flat rates
for cats and other species. Fully backward compatible: existing flat fees
remain the fallback when a rule row is not set.

Backend (Node)
* New util/breedRules.js — curated ~50-breed Large/Aggressive list
  (Rottweiler, Pitbull, German Shepherd, Doberman, Great Dane, Mastiffs,
  Rajapalayam, Tibetan Mastiff, Indian native large breeds, etc.) plus
  classifier that maps (species, breed) -> (bucket, size_category).
* New nigam_fee_rules table + unique index — created idempotently on
  Node boot via the existing migration runner.
* New endpoints (super_admin OR nigam_admin for own nigam):
  - GET  /api/geo/nigams/:id/fee-rules      -> full 4-row matrix
  - PUT  /api/geo/nigams/:id/fee-rules      -> upsert non-empty rows,
                                                delete all-null rows
  - GET  /api/geo/nigams/:id/resolve-fee    -> per-citizen fee preview
    with resolvedFrom ∈ 'rule' | 'nigam' | 'default'

Payment engine (C#)
* ResolveFeeAsync extended to a 4-tier fallback chain:
    1) per-species/size rule from nigam_fee_rules
    2) per-nigam flat fee on the nigams row
    3) appsettings Payment:*Fee override
    4) hard-coded constants
* CreateOrderRequest gains optional Species + Breed. Old callers keep
  working — Species null => tier 2 lookup as before.

Admin UI (wwwroot/js/afp-fees.js)
* Each Nigam card now has a collapsible "Per-species & size rates" panel
  under the existing flat-fee editor:
  - Dog — Large / Aggressive
  - Dog — Small
  - Cat
  - Other
* Empty inputs = no override => the row is deleted server-side, so the
  flat fee wins for that bucket. Same 0–10000 bounds, same audit.
* Both Super Admin and Nigam Admin can edit both sections for the nigams
  they own (unchanged from earlier — matches the flat-fee policy).

Citizen UI (wwwroot/js/afp-pets.js)
* Register New Pet: live per-species/size fee preview banner that
  recomputes whenever species or breed changes.
* Renew Licence: fee updates when a pet is picked, using its species+
  breed for the correct tier (Q5 grandfathering — new rates apply at
  next renewal only).

Tests
* 6 new xUnit tests covering: Large/Aggressive dog uses rule, Small dog
  uses rule, Cat single, Rabbit -> other, no-rule fallback to flat,
  renewal of large dog uses rule renewal fee.
* 42/42 pass, 0 build warnings.

Migrations
* No manual SQL required. Table is created idempotently on Node boot;
  nothing changes for existing rows in nigams. New nigam_fee_rules table
  starts empty so every fee resolves via the existing flat-fee path
  until an admin fills in the matrix.
